How to Optimize for Long-Tail Terms (e.g., "unscramble 7-letter word")

Google only indexes real web pages with unique URLs. You cannot rank for
long-tail keywords just by adding tags to a sitemap—you need landing pages for
them.

Here is how top-ranking word unscramblers (like WordFinder or ScrabbleFinder)
target these long-tail searches:

1. Create Dedicated Landing Pages (Programmatic SEO)

Create dedicated HTML pages or URL routes for high-volume search queries, such
as:

  - https://letterunscramblerpro.com/7-letter-words.html
  - https://letterunscramblerpro.com/6-letter-words.html
  - https://letterunscramblerpro.com/5-letter-words.html
  - https://letterunscramblerpro.com/words-with-z.html

2. Add Unique Content & HTML Titles

On each dedicated page, optimize the <title> tag and <h1> header for that exact
term:

  - Page Title: <title>7 Letter Word Unscrambler - Find All 7-Letter
    Words</title>
  - Main Heading: <h1>Unscramble 7-Letter Words</h1>
  - On-Page Text: Add a short paragraph explaining how to solve 7-letter word
    puzzles, along with popular 7-letter word examples (e.g., ACROSS, BEAUTY,
    CHEESE).

3. Add those new URLs to your Sitemap

Once you build those pages, add them to your sitemap.xml:

  <url>
    <loc>https://letterunscramblerpro.com/7-letter-words.html</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>0.8</priority>
  </url>
